ayload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"db4a0beb831070bef81b1135dafea1cc11bb8c048c3eab1fbb67f9d020c402f0","event_uuid":"e2478a3b-b588-4cd4-9ff5-2aa60327619f","position":{"commit_sha":"bd70762c728e67950833224c4b6137de650831ec","position":"1786597042255162001-e2478a3b-b588-4cd4-9ff5-2aa60327619f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-226_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"e9c8ec02-ef1c-4bee-95c0-2facb4a6fad8","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landing-order note (epic task-dag advisory): children 985c (graph complexity) and b2bb (compact split) both update the GENERATED ratchet file .github/complexity-baseline.json, since each lowers CCN baselines. This is not a semantic conflict — the baseline is regenerated by re-running the baseline command, and Gerrit Rebase-If-Necessary re-derives it on the second change to land. Guidance: whichever lands second must re-run the complexity-baseline regeneration before/at rebase so its entry reflects post-first-change numbers; no explicit blocking edge is added (it would only serialize a mechanically-regenerated file). All other child file_impacts are disjoint.","timestamp":1786242413790821001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OWNERSHIP TRANSFER (operator-ordered, 2026-08-12): this session (6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7) now owns all in-progress epics, including this one (previously session e9c8ec02). Resuming the remediation: dispatching implementers for the open children acouchi (structured_run split), earwig (graph blocker complexity), harrier (attest typing) now; iguana (event_append split) is HELD until the P0 compact-on-close fix (choosy-arthrodic-barbet) lands, since both touch event_append/compaction and would conflict. Landing-order note from prior comments honored: complexity-baseline.json is regenerated per-landing, rebase-regenerate on conflict.","timestamp":1786597042255162001}],"created_at":1786219904383770001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4e1c4ef9-4d05-4c03-88d3-30804d5d974b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ae1b-b2a0-a080-4b4e"}],"description":"## Context\nRemediation epic for the comprehensive quality audit recorded on ae1b-b2a0-a080-4b4e. Scope is deliberately narrowed to three buckets the audit flagged: (1) the CI default-suite reliability flake, (2) the assignee/user-facing documentation bug, and (3) the LOW-RISK, NON-OVERLAPPING slice of the file-size, complexity, and typing findings.\n\n## Architectural principle (avoid recurrence, not just the instance)\nThe near-cap modules and high-CCN functions in scope share one root cause: **flat units that mix responsibilities/layers, plus duplicated infrastructure that every new call-site re-hand-rolls**. The shrink-only ratchets prevent *regression* but not *creep toward the cap*. So each child fixes the cause structurally rather than cutting lines to a number:\n- Decompose by **responsibility/layer with a one-way dependency direction**, so future code has an obvious small home instead of re-inflating a god-file: run-mechanism vs. diagnostics vs. failure-interpretation (structured_run); CLI-facade vs. transaction vs. snapshot-rebuild (compact); public-API vs. recovery vs. git-primitives (event_append).\n- **Centralize duplicated infrastructure WITHOUT changing node-set semantics**: the graph child promotes the 15-line _loader.py shim into a real loader+traversal layer (a `load_indexed_states` applied only where the reduce/index policy is provably identical — _blockers & _compute_dep_graph — plus a pure shared `bfs` skeleton the raw-reduce BFS functions reuse while keeping their exact traversal), removing the duplicated loop that drives the CCN without altering any function's result set.\n- **Preserve public import paths** (re-export moved public symbols) so every extraction stays behavior-identical and touches only non-contended files.\n\nSplits follow existing call-graph seams (AGENTS.md module-size policy); new modules are >=100 LOC; complexity baselines move downward only.\n\n## Scope selection (why these and not others)\nNon-overlap computed against the file_impact of all 212 in-progress tickets (audit ticket excluded); every NEW child touches only zero-contention files. Deliberately EXCLUDED:\n- High-risk complexity orchestrators next_batch.compute (CCN 42) and import_ndjson.import_tickets (CCN 45) — core scheduling/import logic, not low-risk.\n- The typing ratchet FLIP in pyproject.toml (contended x9) and the near-cap files runner.py/_config_schema.py/signing.py/_ref_lock.py/init.py (all contended).\n- Already-tracked, out-of-requested-scope findings: mutmut lane (521b-04c3-572f-4514), repo-wide package DAG (44ea-43c6-b351-4d81), test-env hardening (def1-9c3c-6802-48bd).\n\n## Recommended systemic follow-up (out of scope here)\nThe ratchets fire only AT the 800 cap / at the recorded CCN. A genuine recurrence guard is an EARLY-WARNING margin (advisory surfaced in the metrics lane at, e.g., ~650 LOC / CCN ~15) so creep is visible before it reaches the cap. That changes enforcement policy and touches the (contended) gate/CI config, so it belongs in its own proposal, not these non-overlapping stories.\n\n## Children\n- Adopted existing open tickets: fade-ea90-7564-4715 (CI flake bug) and 879f-5549-91e3-4d6f (user-facing doc drift incl. the assignee example).\n- New non-overlapping tasks: split near-cap modules structured_run.py / compact.py / event_append.py; centralize graph loader/traversal to cut blocker-subsystem complexity; annotate the attest package to be typing-ratchet-ready.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] CI flake fade-ea90 resolved (or root-caused with a durable fix) so the Python 3.11 xdist worker no longer dies in test_opcert_service_app.\n- [ ] User-facing assignee example teaches a Jira-resolvable identity consistent with docs/config.md.\n- [ ] The three named near-cap modules are split by responsibility along existing call-graph seams with public import paths preserved, and each ends with real headroom under the 800 cap: structured_run.py and compact.py reach the ≤500 target, and event_append.py drops to ≤640 (its git-primitive leaf extracted; recovery kept with the API to preserve the monkeypatch/test seam that couples their shared `_git_add` patch point).\n- [ ] The graph loader/traversal duplication is centralized and the four flagged functions drop to their target CCN with graph outputs unchanged.\n- [ ] The attest package is clean under mypy src/rebar/attest --disallow-untyped-defs (ratchet flip deferred to when pyproject.toml contention clears).\n- [ ] Every new child edited only non-in-progress-contended files.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py","reason":"file-size split"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact.py","reason":"file-size split + complexity"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/event_append.py","reason":"file-size split"},{"path":"src/rebar/graph","reason":"blocker-subsystem complexity reduction"},{"path":"src/rebar/attest","reason":"typing annotations"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"aa207830-7fc8-45b4-95cb-107cfa0c8614","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["remediation","audit","ae1b"],"ticket_id":"2fe0-ce8b-4715-4e07","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Remediation (audit ae1b): CI-flake, assignee doc bug, and low-risk non-overlapping size/complexity/typing debt","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d49a9c28-ca0c-4927-a321-2e52d617b93b","e6a6ac70-2e0a-430f-87fe-da0429785d6a","4e1c4ef9-4d05-4c03-88d3-30804d5d974b","096721e7-4fb1-44a6-b797-93e0abd33bb1","8f2c60de-6434-4793-8c5d-3a75d00e96a5","ae97335c-1a3a-4462-8cb5-c52a0e3166ac","abe11d0a-c847-417b-8d9f-9ad35a471876","b480904d-c392-4c08-b59a-add2cb96a8e2","aa207830-7fc8-45b4-95cb-107cfa0c8614","98aa7d74-a58e-43a1-938f-e226ccfa9d80","e2478a3b-b588-4cd4-9ff5-2aa60327619f"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659547147882001,"uuid":"3be37bee-109f-40a7-aaaf-5d96bd81ebc2"}